---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Bend Oregon SEO Consultant | Local SEO Services in Bend, OR"
  description="SEO consulting for Bend, Oregon businesses that want better Google rankings, stronger local search visibility, more qualified leads, and a clearer strategy for SEO and AI search."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Bend Oregon SEO Services</p>

          <h1>SEO help for Bend businesses that want to get found.</h1>

          <p class="hero-text">
            I help Bend businesses improve Google visibility, local search performance,
            website structure, content strategy, and search-driven leads.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-buttons">
            <a href="/contact/" class="primary-btn">Contact Me About Bend SEO</a>
            <a href="/services/ai-search" class="secondary-btn">AI Search Strategy</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="visibility-card">
          <p class="card-label">Bend SEO Visibility</p>

          <div class="dashboard-list">
            <div class="dashboard-row">
              <span>Google Search</span>
              <span class="status active">Priority</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dashboard-row">
              <span>Google Maps</span>
              <span class="status active">Local</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dashboard-row">
              <span>Service Pages</span>
              <span class="status active">Core</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dashboard-row">
              <span>Technical SEO</span>
              <span class="status active">Foundation</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dashboard-row">
              <span>Content Strategy</span>
              <span class="status warning">Opportunity</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dashboard-row">
              <span>AI Search</span>
              <span class="status warning">Growing</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="dashboard-summary">
            <div>
              <strong>Bend</strong>
              <span>Local Focus</span>
            </div>

            <div>
              <strong>SEO + AI</strong>
              <span>Search Strategy</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="intro">
      <div class="container intro-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Local search strategy</p>
          <h2>People are searching before they call, book, visit, or buy.</h2>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p>
            Bend is a competitive local market. People use Google to find everything from
            contractors and healthcare providers to restaurants, real estate professionals,
            outdoor experiences, local shops, and professional services.
          </p>

          <p>
            I help Bend businesses build stronger SEO foundations, improve local visibility,
            and turn search traffic into calls, leads, bookings, visits, and revenue.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-label">SEO for Bend businesses</p>
          <h2>Local visibility matters when someone is ready to take action.</h2>

          <p>
            A person searching for a plumber in Bend, a place to eat near the Old Mill,
            a local dentist, a wedding photographer, a property manager, or an outdoor
            experience already has a need. Good SEO helps put your business in front of
            that person at the right moment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="service-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">01</span>
            <h3>Get Found by Local Customers</h3>
            <p>
              Improve visibility when people in Bend search for the exact services,
              products, or experiences your business offers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">02</span>
            <h3>Compete Beyond Your Business Name</h3>
            <p>
              Ranking for your own business name is important, but SEO helps you reach
              people who have never heard of you and are still deciding who to choose.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">03</span>
            <h3>Reach Visitors and New Residents</h3>
            <p>
              Bend businesses can serve longtime locals, people new to Central Oregon,
              and visitors actively searching for places to go, things to do, and businesses
              to trust.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">04</span>
            <h3>Turn Search Visibility Into Business</h3>
            <p>
              The goal is not traffic for the sake of traffic. It is attracting the right
              people and making it easy for them to call, book, visit, request a quote,
              or take the next step.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about">
      <div class="container about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Real local search behavior</p>
          <h2>What are people actually searching for in Bend?</h2>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p>
            Local searches come in many forms. Some people know exactly what they need.
            Others are comparing options, looking for recommendations, or trying to solve
            a problem.
          </p>

          <p>
            Depending on the business, that could mean searches like
            <strong> HVAC repair Bend Oregon</strong>,
            <strong> family dentist near me</strong>,
            <strong> Bend wedding photographer</strong>,
            <strong> best restaurants in Bend</strong>,
            <strong> property management Bend Oregon</strong>, or
            <strong> things to do in Bend with kids</strong>.
          </p>

          <p>
            The right SEO strategy identifies the searches that actually matter to your
            business and builds pages, content, and local signals around them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Local industries</p>
          <h2>SEO for businesses across Bend and Central Oregon.</h2>

          <p>
            Different businesses need different search strategies. A contractor trying to
            generate service calls should not approach SEO the same way as a restaurant,
            healthcare practice, real estate business, or tourism company.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="service-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">01</span>
            <h3>Contractors & Home Services</h3>
            <p>
              SEO for plumbers, electricians, HVAC companies, landscapers, cleaners,
              painters, roofers, remodelers, and other businesses serving Bend homeowners.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">02</span>
            <h3>Healthcare & Wellness</h3>
            <p>
              Local search strategies for dentists, chiropractors, physical therapists,
              wellness providers, medical practices, and other healthcare professionals.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">03</span>
            <h3>Real Estate & Property Services</h3>
            <p>
              Search visibility for real estate agents, property managers, builders,
              inspectors, mortgage professionals, and businesses serving buyers,
              sellers, renters, and homeowners.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">04</span>
            <h3>Restaurants, Breweries & Food</h3>
            <p>
              Help people discover local restaurants, coffee shops, breweries,
              food businesses, and other places to eat and drink around Bend.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">05</span>
            <h3>Outdoor Recreation & Tourism</h3>
            <p>
              SEO for guides, rentals, tours, lodging, outdoor brands, recreation
              companies, and businesses serving people exploring Bend and Central Oregon.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">06</span>
            <h3>Professional Services</h3>
            <p>
              Search strategy for attorneys, accountants, consultants, agencies,
              financial professionals, and other businesses that depend on qualified leads.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">07</span>
            <h3>Local Shops & Retail</h3>
            <p>
              Help Bend retailers and local brands become easier to discover through
              Google Search, Maps, product-focused content, and useful local information.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">08</span>
            <h3>Small & Growing Businesses</h3>
            <p>
              Practical SEO guidance for local businesses that need to figure out what
              will actually make a difference without wasting time or budget.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="scorecard">
      <div class="container scorecard-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">SEO visibility check</p>
          <h2>How visible is your Bend business in search?</h2>

          <p>
            I can review how your business shows up across Google, local map results,
            your website pages, technical SEO, content, and AI search opportunities.
          </p>

          <a href="/contact/" class="primary-btn">Request a Bend SEO Review</a>
        </div>

        <div class="scorecard-panel">
          <div class="score-row">
            <span>Google Search</span>
            <strong>Organic visibility</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="score-row">
            <span>Google Maps</span>
            <strong>Local discovery</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="score-row">
            <span>Google Business Profile</span>
            <strong>Local trust</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="score-row">
            <span>Website Pages</span>
            <strong>Service clarity</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="score-row">
            <span>Technical SEO</span>
            <strong>Crawlability</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="score-row">
            <span>Content Strategy</span>
            <strong>Search intent coverage</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-label">What I help with</p>
          <h2>Practical SEO support for Bend, Oregon businesses.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="service-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">01</span>
            <h3>Local SEO Strategy</h3>
            <p>
              Improve how your business appears for Bend-area searches, map results,
              service terms, and high-intent local keywords.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">02</span>
            <h3>Website SEO</h3>
            <p>
              Strengthen title tags, page structure, internal links, headings,
              crawlability, and the content signals search engines use to understand your site.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">03</span>
            <h3>Content Planning</h3>
            <p>
              Build service pages, location pages, guides, and supporting content
              that bring in people looking for exactly what you offer.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">04</span>
            <h3>Google Business Profile</h3>
            <p>
              Improve the accuracy, completeness, and local relevance of one of the most
              important parts of your visibility in Google Maps and local search.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">05</span>
            <h3>Technical SEO</h3>
            <p>
              Find and fix issues involving crawling, indexing, redirects, internal links,
              page performance, structured data, and overall site architecture.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">06</span>
            <h3>Reporting & Strategy</h3>
            <p>
              Use organic traffic, leads, rankings, search visibility, and business results
              to decide what to fix, improve, and build next.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">07</span>
            <h3>Competitor Research</h3>
            <p>
              Understand which local competitors are appearing in search, what they rank for,
              where they are strong, and where your business has opportunities to compete.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <span class="card-number">08</span>
            <h3>AI Search Visibility</h3>
            <p>
              Prepare your website and broader online presence to be understood and
              discovered through AI assistants and evolving search experiences.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="intro">
      <div class="container intro-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Bend search seasonality</p>
          <h2>Search demand can change throughout the year.</h2>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p>
            Bend is not a one-season market. Summer travel, winter recreation, home
            improvement projects, weddings, moving, dining, events, and outdoor activities
            can all create different search opportunities throughout the year.
          </p>

          <p>
            For some businesses, SEO should account for that seasonality. That could mean
            improving important pages before peak demand arrives, publishing useful content
            early enough for Google to discover it, and looking at year-over-year trends
            instead of treating every month exactly the same.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about">
      <div class="container about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Bend and Central Oregon</p>
          <h2>Your customers may search beyond one city name.</h2>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p>
            Some Bend businesses serve a very specific part of town. Others work throughout
            Central Oregon. The right strategy depends on where you actually do business
            and where your customers come from.
          </p>

          <p>
            That can include searches related to Downtown Bend, the Old Mill District,
            Northwest Crossing, East Bend, and other parts of the city, as well as nearby
            communities such as Redmond, Sisters, Sunriver, La Pine, and Prineville when
            those locations are genuinely part of your service area.
          </p>

          <p>
            I focus on building useful pages around real services and real locations rather
            than creating thin, repetitive location pages just to target more keywords.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="search-everywhere">
      <div class="container search-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label light">Beyond rankings</p>
          <h2>Good SEO should support real business goals.</h2>

          <p>
            Rankings matter, but they are not the whole point. The real goal is getting
            in front of the right people and helping them take the next step.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="channel-grid">
          <div>Local Searches</div>
          <div>Google Maps</div>
          <div>Service Pages</div>
          <div>Reviews</div>
          <div>Local Content</div>
          <div>AI Search</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about">
      <div class="container about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Bend-based SEO support</p>
          <h2>Local search strategy with a Central Oregon perspective.</h2>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p>
            I live in Central Oregon and understand how people search for local businesses here.
            That matters when thinking about Bend neighborhoods, nearby towns, seasonal demand,
            tourism, outdoor recreation, home services, local competition, and the way people
            discover businesses throughout the region.
          </p>

          <p>
            My work focuses on making your website clearer, more useful, and easier to find.
            That can include local SEO, technical fixes, content planning, keyword research,
            internal linking, Google Business Profile strategy, reporting, and AI search readiness.
          </p>

          <p>
            I also believe in keeping SEO understandable. You should know what is being worked on,
            why it matters, and how it connects to actual business goals.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Bend SEO FAQs</p>
          <h2>Common questions about SEO for local businesses.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="service-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Does my Bend business really need SEO?</h3>
            <p>
              If potential customers use Google to find, research, or compare businesses
              like yours, SEO can help. The opportunity depends on your industry,
              competition, website, service area, and how people search for what you offer.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>What is the difference between SEO and local SEO?</h3>
            <p>
              SEO improves your overall visibility in organic search. Local SEO places
              additional focus on geographic searches, Google Maps, your Google Business
              Profile, reviews, local relevance, and searches from people near your business
              or within your service area.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Should I target Bend or all of Central Oregon?</h3>
            <p>
              That depends on where you genuinely serve customers. Some businesses should
              focus heavily on Bend. Others may have opportunities in Redmond, Sisters,
              Sunriver, La Pine, Prineville, or throughout Central Oregon.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>How long does SEO take?</h3>
            <p>
              There is no single timeline. Some improvements can have an impact relatively
              quickly, while competitive searches and larger growth strategies can take
              months. The starting condition of your website, competition, authority,
              technical issues, and content all matter.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Can you help with Google Maps and my Google Business Profile?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Local SEO can include reviewing your Google Business Profile, business
              categories, services, website connections, local landing pages, reviews,
              and overall Google Maps visibility.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Can SEO help my business appear in AI search?</h3>
            <p>
              Strong SEO creates an important foundation for AI search visibility.
              Clear website structure, useful content, strong brand signals, crawlability,
              authority, and accurate information can all help search engines and AI systems
              better understand your business.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="section-label">Ready to improve local visibility?</p>
        <h2>Let’s make your Bend business easier to find.</h2>

        <p>
          Whether you need local SEO help, a website SEO audit, better service pages,
          Google Business Profile guidance, or a clearer search strategy, I can help
          you figure out what to focus on next.
        </p>

        <a href="/contact/" class="primary-btn">Contact Me About Bend SEO</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
